READINGS = [
    dict(stem="syndicate_2008_2015", verdict="correct", pages=[36, 5], filing=-8.228,
         finding=True, takeon_amount=85.227, gross_opening=308.138,
         carried="note 16's gross roll-forward books 'RITC take on reserves 85,227' directly after the 1 January balance, and the adopted 'Change in prior year provisions' line follows it in the same roll-forward; the whole take-on row is covered",
         quote="""p36 note 16 'Technical provisions', 2015, gross / reinsurance / net (£000): 'Balance at 1 January 308,138 (81,579) 226,560'; 'RITC take on reserves 85,227 (25,564) 59,663'; 'Change in prior year provisions (8,228) (7,808) (16,036)'; 'Claims paid during the year (63,993) 20,228 (43,765)'; 'Effect of movements in exchange rates 6,783 (3,586) 3,198'; 'Balance at 31 December 327,927 (98,307) 229,620'. p5: 'As at 1 January 2015: syndicate 1965's 2011 and prior years of account and syndicate 2243's 2012 and prior years of account have been reinsured.'; 'Total net reserves taken on equate to the RITC premiums paid to the syndicate and amounted to £65.8m.'""",
         why="""Take-on base: true; covered amount 85.227m. The verdict: the adopted -8.2 is note 16's gross 'Change in prior year provisions' (8,228), a stated movement (rule 2). The difference, 0.028, is inside max(0.5, 0.41) = 0.5. Correct. The roll-forward closes: 308,138 + 85,227 - 8,228 - 63,993 + 6,783 = 327,927. The take-on: Syndicates 1965 (2011 and prior) and 2243 (2012 and prior) were reinsured to close into 2008 as at 1 January 2015 (p5). Note 16 books them as 'RITC take on reserves 85,227' directly after the 1 January balance, and the adopted prior-year line follows in the same roll-forward. So the line covers the business taken on, and the adopted opening reserves, 308,138 at 1 January, exclude it. The transfer is inward and in the report year. It did not come from a quota-share reinsurer of 2008's own business, and it sits in no column or line without development. The gross amount is the take-on row, 85,227. (p5's £65.8m of net reserves taken on differs from the net row, 59,663; the repair uses the gross row.) Severity -2.66% on the opening reserves; -2.08% with 85.227m. Opening 308,138 (p36), as adopted."""),
    dict(stem="syndicate_2008_2016", verdict="correct", pages=[40, 7], filing=-12.896,
         finding=True, takeon_amount=148.677, gross_opening=327.957,
         carried="note 15's gross roll-forward books 'RITC take on reserves 148,677' directly after the 1 January balance, and the adopted 'Change in prior year provisions' line follows it; the roll-forward has no other row, so the take-on row holds both the 2468 RITC and the new IPH quota share; the whole row is covered",
         quote="""p40 note 15 'Technical provisions', 2016, gross / reinsurance / net (£000): 'Balance at 1 January 327,957 (98,307) 229,620'; 'RITC take on reserves 148,677 (21,710) 126,967'; 'Change in prior year provisions (12,896) (2,227) (15,123)'; 'Claims paid during the year (57,070) 11,328 (45,742)'; 'Effect of movements in exchange rates 44,618 (14,538) 30,081'; 'Balance at 31 December 451,287 (125,453) 325,804'. p7: 'As at 1 January 2016: syndicate 2468's 2007 and prior years of account were reinsured and a 100% quota share agreement on its 2008 Italian Public Hospital (IPH) liabilities was written.'; 'Total net reserves taken on equate to the RITC premiums paid to the syndicate and amounted to £127.0m.'""",
         why="""Take-on base: true; covered amount 148.677m. The verdict: the adopted -12.896 is note 15's gross 'Change in prior year provisions' (12,896), rule 2, exact. Correct. The roll-forward closes to 451,286 against a printed 451,287. The take-on: Syndicate 2468's 2007 and prior years of account were reinsured to close into 2008 as at 1 January 2016, and 2008 wrote a 100% quota share of 2468's 2008 IPH liabilities (p7). Note 15 books 'RITC take on reserves 148,677' after the 1 January balance, and the adopted prior-year line follows in the same roll-forward, so it covers the business taken on. The opening reserves, 327,957, exclude it. The roll-forward has no other row that could carry the quota share's reserves, so the take-on row holds both transfers; its net amount, 126,967, is the £127.0m p7 states. Both are inward and new in 2016. 2008 is the quota-share reinsurer here, not the cedant, so the exclusion for a quota-share reinsurer of the syndicate's own business does not apply. Severity -3.93% on the opening reserves; -2.71% with 148.677m. Opening 327,957 (p40), as adopted."""),
    dict(stem="syndicate_2008_2018", verdict="correct", pages=[48, 7], filing=0.002,
         finding=True, takeon_amount=1251.064, gross_opening=369.552,
         carried="note 17's gross roll-forward books 'RITC take on reserves 1,251,064' directly after the 1 January balance, and the adopted 'Change in prior year provisions' line follows it; the stated take-on row is an upper bound, since the commuted 2016 IPH quota share's reserves may be inside it and the filing states no amount for them",
         quote="""p48 note 17 'Technical provisions', gross / reinsurance / net (£000), 2018: 'Balance at 1 January 369,552 (90,090) 279,462'; 'RITC take on reserves 1,251,064 (291,480) 959,584'; 'Change in prior year provisions 2 (411) (409)'; 'Claims paid during the year (312,676) 89,550 (223,126)'; 'Effect of movements in exchange rates 23,548 (6,974) 16,574'; 'Balance at 31 December 1,331,490 (299,405) 1,032,085'; 2017: 'Balance at 1 January 451,287'; 'RITC take on reserves - - -'. p7: 'As at 1 January 2016: Syndicate 2468's 2007 and prior years of account were reinsured and a 100% quota share agreement on its 2008 Italian Public Hospital (IPH) liabilities was written.'; 'There were no RITC transactions in 2017.'; 'As at 1 January 2018: Syndicate 2007's 2015 and prior years of account and Syndicate 2468's 2008 to 2015 year of account were reinsured. The 2016 year of account 100% quota share agreement with S2468 on its 2008 year of account IPH liabilities was commuted.'""",
         why="""Take-on base: true; covered amount 1,251.064m, the stated take-on row and an upper bound. The verdict: the adopted +0.002 is note 17's gross 'Change in prior year provisions' (2), rule 2, exact. Correct. The roll-forward closes: 369,552 + 1,251,064 + 2 - 312,676 + 23,548 = 1,331,490. The take-on: Syndicate 2007's 2015 and prior years of account and Syndicate 2468's 2008-2015 years of account were reinsured to close into 2008 as at 1 January 2018 (p7). Note 17 books 'RITC take on reserves 1,251,064' after the 1 January balance, and the adopted prior-year line follows in the same roll-forward, so it covers that business. The opening reserves, 369,552, exclude it. One part may already be in the opening reserves. The 100% quota share of 2468's 2008 IPH liabilities, written in 2016, was commuted when 2468's 2008 year came in (p7). The roll-forward has no commutation row, and the filing states no amount for the quota share's reserves. If the take-on row is gross of them (the commutation settled through claims paid), the business the opening excludes is smaller by that unstated amount. So 1,251.064m is the amount the filing states, and an upper bound. Severity +0.0005% on the opening reserves; +0.0001% with 1,251.064m. Opening 369,552 (p48), as adopted."""),
    dict(stem="syndicate_2008_2019", verdict="correct", pages=[50, 7], filing=14.053,
         finding=True, takeon_amount=701.118, gross_opening=1331.49,
         carried="note 17's gross roll-forward books 'RITC take on reserves 701,118' directly after the 1 January balance, and the adopted 'Change in prior year provisions' line follows it (the form the ninth amendment names); the stated take-on row is an upper bound, since 2008 has reinsured 5820's 2010 motor book 100% since 2013 and the filing states no amount for it; the Cavello Bay quota share is outward",
         quote="""p50 note 17 'Technical provisions', gross / reinsurance / net (£000), 2019: 'Balance at 1 January 1,331,490 (299,405) 1,032,085'; 'RITC take on reserves 701,118 (199,540) 501,578'; 'Change in prior year provisions 14,053 (611,544) (597,491)'; 'Claims paid during the year (403,131) 131,149 (271,982)'; 'Effect of movements in exchange rates (50,076) 20,885 (29,191)'; 'Balance at 31 December 1,593,454 (958,455) 634,999'. p7: 'As at 1 January 2013: Syndicate 1231's 2009 and prior years of account were reinsured, and there was a 100% quota share reinsurance agreement with Syndicate 5820 in respect of its motor book on the 2010 underwriting year.'; 'As at 1 January 2019: Syndicates 2526, 1206, 1861 and 5820's 2016 and prior years of account were reinsured.'; 'Effective 1 October 2019, the Syndicate entered into a 50% quota share agreement with Cavello Bay Reinsurance Limited (a subsidiary of Enstar Group Limited). The contract is applicable to both the 2018 and 2019 years of account and is a reinsurance of the net results of each underwriting year.'""",
         why="""Take-on base: true; covered amount 701.118m, the stated take-on row and an upper bound. The verdict: the adopted (confirmed) +14.053 is note 17's gross 'Change in prior year provisions' (14,053), rule 2, exact. Correct. The roll-forward closes: 1,331,490 + 701,118 + 14,053 - 403,131 - 50,076 = 1,593,454. The take-on: Syndicates 2526, 1206, 1861 and 5820's 2016 and prior years of account were reinsured to close into 2008 as at 1 January 2019 (p7). Note 17 books 'RITC take on reserves 701,118' after the 1 January balance, and the adopted prior-year line follows it in the same roll-forward, the form the ninth amendment names. The opening reserves, 1,331,490, exclude it. The Cavello Bay quota share is outward, a reinsurance of 2008's own 2018 and 2019 years, and its recoveries sit in the reinsurance column, so it adds nothing. One part may already be in the opening reserves. 2008 has reinsured 100% of 5820's 2010 motor book since 2013, and 5820's 2010 year came in with its other years. The filing records no commutation and states no amount for that book. So 701.118m is the amount the filing states, and an upper bound. Severity +1.06% on the opening reserves; +0.69% with 701.118m. Opening 1,331,490 (p50), as adopted."""),
    dict(stem="syndicate_2008_2023", verdict="correct", pages=[49, 50, 41, 6, 52], filing=79.213,
         finding=True, takeon_amount=234.962, gross_opening=1186.259,
         carried="Syndicate 1301's business, taken on at 1 January 2023, is carried on both diagonals of the step: the 2019 and 2020 columns, which of the recorded transactions only 1301's covers, print every value from the end of their first year and move by +12,950 and -1,303 in 2023, and no column jumps in 2023; 1301's years before 2014 sit in the provision in respect of prior years, which has no development rows, and the filing does not split the 234,962, so it is an upper bound; the QBE LPT is the 2023 column and the 1492 RITC converts a 2022 LPT the opening holds",
         quote="""p49 note 17 'Claims development', 'Estimate of ultimate gross claims' (£000; 2014-2023): 'At end of underwriting year 51,178 64,515 72,587 121,378 102,089 55,412 83,037 1,606,621 - 363,165'; 'One year later 89,737 109,901 147,537 241,414 185,243 107,046 88,963 1,638,140'; 'Two years later 88,990 120,047 166,367 265,607 205,674 116,808 64,256 1,682,777'; 'Three years later 85,731 1,021,653 733,262 266,397 203,613 113,262 62,953'; 'Four years later 989,173 1,198,950 757,828 269,852 282,351 126,212'; 'Five years later 1,086,445 1,205,372 767,336 386,601 277,975'; 'Six years later 1,080,573 1,199,692 852,391 388,040'; 'Seven years later 1,067,606 1,211,401 855,177'; 'Eight years later 1,061,374 1,249,079'; 'Nine years later 1,046,776'; 'Provision in respect of prior years 421,573'; 'The calendar year developments in the tables above include the impact of reserves newly acquired through RITC and LPT transactions.' p50 note 18, 2023 gross: 'Balance at 1 January 1,186,259'; 'RITC take on reserves 234,962'; 'Change in prior year provisions 388,016'; 'Change in prior year provisions also include the take-on balances of the LPT contract with QBE amounting to £319.0m'. p41: 'The above movements also include the take-on balances of the RITC with Syndicate 1301 (amounting to £235.0m Gross and £158.0m Net) and LPT contract with QBE (amounting to £319.0m Gross and £159.5m Net).' p6: 'In February 2023, the Syndicate entered into an RITC agreement with Probitas Managing Agency Limited for Syndicate 1492, reinsuring their 2018 and prior years of account (YOA). This was a conversion of a 2022 calendar year LPT into an RITC.'; 'Syndicate 2008 assumed Syndicate 1301's assets and liabilities in respect of the 2020 and prior YOAs with effect from 1 January 2023.' p52: 'QBE LPT business that has been reported in the 2023 YOA'. syndicate_2008_2021 p53, 'Pure underwriting year - Gross': columns 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016 and 2021 only; 2014 'Four years later 717,029' (no earlier value), 'Seven years later 944,592'.""",
         why="""Take-on base: true; covered amount at most 234.962m. The verdict: triangle route, rule 1 over underwriting years up to 2021: -14,598 + 37,678 + 2,786 + 1,439 - 4,376 + 12,950 - 1,303 + 44,637 = +79,213 GBP000, equal to the adopted figure. Note 18's gross prior-year line (388,016, with the QBE take-on inside it) is a stated movement; recorded, not scored. Correct. The take-on: three 2023 transactions. (1) The QBE LPT (319.0m gross) is reported in the 2023 year of account (p52) and sits in the report year's own column (363,165 gross, 181,582 net), outside the step. (2) The 1492 RITC converts a 2022 LPT, which the opening reserves already hold (p6), and books no take-on row. (3) Syndicate 1301's 2020 and prior years came in on 1 January 2023, booked as 'RITC take on reserves 234,962' after the 1 January balance, 1,186,259, which excludes them. The table carries 1301's business on both diagonals of the step. Of the transactions this filing and the 2021 report record, only 1301's covers the 2019 and 2020 underwriting years: 1492's years are 2018 and prior, the QBE business is in the 2023 column, and the 2021 report prints no 2017-2020 columns. Yet here the 2019 and 2020 columns print every value from the end of their first year (2019: 55,412, reaching 113,262 at the end of 2022; 2020: 83,037, then 64,256), and they move by +12,950 and -1,303 in 2023. The 2014-2016 columns likewise print values from before 2018 (2014: 51,178 at the end of 2014) that the 2021 report does not (its 2014 column starts at 717,029 at the end of 2018). So the table restates 1301's history. Earlier acquisitions enter in the year they came in, as note 17 says: 2014 and 2015 jump by about 900m in 2018 (85,731 to 989,173; 120,047 to 1,021,653), 2016 by 567m in 2019, and 2016-2018 by 85,055, 116,749 and 78,738 in 2022 (the 1492 LPT). No column jumps in 2023. This supersedes my eighth-census reading, which placed all of 1301's business in the provision in respect of prior years. Part of it may still sit there: 1301's years before 2014 have no columns, and that line has no development rows. The filing does not split the 234,962, and the 2022 report is not in the corpus. So 234.962m is an upper bound on the covered amount. Severity 6.68% on the opening reserves; 5.57% with 234.962m. Opening 1,186,259 (p50), as adopted."""),
    dict(stem="syndicate_1084_2014", verdict="correct", pages=[26, 30, 11, 4], filing=-77.4,
         finding=True, takeon_amount=131.7, gross_opening=1332.5,
         carried="note 4's release is the 2014 movement in the syndicate's provision for claims outstanding in respect of prior periods, which from 1 January 2014 includes Syndicate 4000's liabilities; note 15 books the 4000 RITC as an acceptance after the 1 January balance; the filing names no exclusion",
         quote="""p26 note 4 'Movement in prior year's provision for claims outstanding': 'During 2014 the Syndicate released £77.4m of technical reserves in respect of prior periods, arising predominantly from the Marine, Property and Treaty Divisions (2013: £79.4m, primarily from the Energy and Treaty Divisions). These releases were due to favourable claims development on losses in 2014.' p30 note 15 'Technical reserves', gross (£m; unearned premiums / claims outstanding / total): 'At 1 January 2014 481.8 1,332.5 1,814.3'; 'Acceptance of Syndicate 4000 RITC - 131.7 131.7'; 'Exchange differences 13.0 46.9 59.9'; 'Claims paid in year - (420.0) (420.0)'; 'Movement in provision 6.6 488.1 481.5'; 'At 31 December 2014 488.2 1,579.2 2,067.4'. p11: 'With effect from 1 January 2014, the Syndicate assumed the liabilities of Syndicate 4000 under a Reinsurance to Close contract, which consisted primarily of Specialist Lines business written by the Syndicate between 2004 and 2008. The transaction resulted in the transfer to Syndicate 1084 of gross and net technical provisions of £131.7m and £92.0m respectively.' p4, 2014 'Underwriting profit / (loss)' by division (Energy, Property, Marine, Aviation, Casualty, Treaty, UK, Run off, Total): '7.2 8.2 18.8 5.0 (8.5) 41.0 (1.0) 5.1 75.8'.""",
         why="""Take-on base: true; covered amount 131.7m. The verdict: the adopted -77.4 is note 4's stated release, rule 2, exact. Note 4 states no basis, and nothing makes plain that it is net. Correct. The take-on: Syndicate 4000's liabilities, mainly Specialist Lines business written in 2004-2008, came into 1084 on 1 January 2014, with gross technical provisions of £131.7m, all claims outstanding (p11, p30). Note 15 books them as an acceptance after the 1 January balance, outside the technical account, so the opening reserves, 1,332.5, exclude them. Note 4's release is the 2014 movement in the syndicate's provision for claims outstanding in respect of prior periods. From 1 January 2014 that provision includes 4000's business, so the release covers any 2014 movement on it, as 609/2014's reassessment of underwriting years 2011 and prior covers Syndicate 570's. The narrative names the divisions that released most, not a business it left out. None of the ninth amendment's exclusions applies: the business is not the report year's, sits in no line without development, came in during the report year, is inward, and did not come from a quota-share reinsurer of 1084. The amount the filing states is 131.7m. Severity -5.81% on the opening reserves; -5.29% with 131.7m. Opening 1,332.5 (p30), as adopted."""),
]
